.pio
.clinerules
CLAUDE.md
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.VSCodeCounter/
.gitignore
.cache/
# Claude Code config is COMMITTED (hooks/rules/skills survive a clone, like
# canon_lint). Only host/session-local state stays out.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/.rfc-ticket
.claude/skills/run-slopdrive-32/
.claude/workflows/
# Serena MCP project cache (host-local symbol index)
.serena/

# Real secrets - never commit. Use secrets.example.h as the shared template.
include/secrets.h
secrets.h

# IDF managed components — ~440 MB fetched into the project root by the
# component manager once custom_sdkconfig turned on the hybrid IDF build
# (platformio.ini, env:s3_main). Generated, never edited by hand, never
# committed. dependencies.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: it pins the exact
# component versions an IDF-from-source build resolves, so tracking it is the
# only way two checkouts build the same image.
managed_components/
# Derived from platformio.ini's custom_sdkconfig block by the hybrid IDF build.
# platformio.ini is the one home for those values (C-1); these are its output.
sdkconfig.defaults
sdkconfig.sd32-ota
sdkconfig.*
.dummy/

# WebUI build artifacts — generated by build_webui.py at compile time :3
webui/node_modules/
webui/dist/
webui/.env.local
# Vite rewrites its config to a timestamped temp file on each start and does
# not always clean up after a killed dev server.
webui/vite.config.*.timestamp-*.mjs

# LittleFS data artifacts — generated by build pipeline, not hand-edited
data/index.html
data/index.html.gz

# Dev tools & diagnostic scripts — not part of the firmware.
# (tools/* not tools/ so specific files CAN be re-included below —
#  git cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory.)
tools/*
# SlopCanon mechanical floor (.claude/rules/governance.md §5) — doctrine enforcement
# is part of the repo, not a scratch script.
!tools/canon_lint.py
# Reversal step-loss ladder. The open DIR-drift issues on the dev board cite
# its rows as evidence, and an issue naming a script that does not survive a
# clone is a dead reference, so this one is tracked. Its OUTPUT is not: that
# goes to artifacts/dir_ladder.json like every other instrument.
!tools/dir_ladder.py
# clangd/Serena compile database generator. PlatformIO's own compiledb target
# emits zero first-party TUs for this ESP-IDF project, so without this script
# symbol search goes silently blind (headers parse as C). Two rules files name
# it as THE regen command, so it has to survive a clone. Its OUTPUT
# (compile_commands.json) stays ignored.
!tools/gen_clangd_db.py
# Spec drift detector (/drift): diffs this repo's protocol reality against
# the pinned SlopSync sibling; its output is the RFC backlog. Tracked for the
# same reason as canon_lint: enforcement tooling survives a clone.
!tools/spec-drift.sh
# CHANNEL-MAP.md table codegen — this repo's own machine-catalog lockstep
# tool: it parses registry.yaml (now the pinned SlopSync sibling's copy) +
# SlopSyncCatalog.h (this device's own channels) so the doc can never
# silently drift from the wire again after the RFC-047 renumber.
!tools/gen_channel_map.py
# Channel-space grid VISUAL generator (RFC-047 companion; output is generated
# per-run evidence, gitignored below).
!tools/gen_channel_grid.py
# platformio.ini names this as pre:tools/ota_auth.py in every -ota env, so a
# clone without it cannot build ANY over-the-air target. It reads the password
# out of include/secrets.h at build time and holds no secret of its own.
!tools/ota_auth.py
# DOCTRINE and TRAPS T-nn treat catalog_lint as binding doctrine enforcement,
# same standing as canon_lint.
!tools/catalog_lint.py
# The /logs viewer: page source, its self-check, and the generator that bakes
# it into C5 flash. platformio.ini names the generator as a c5_probe pre-script,
# so it is load-bearing build machinery, not a scratch instrument.
!tools/gen_logview_header.py
!tools/logview/
# The RP2350 A/B partition table (sd-4k1.3). Not an instrument: the firmware's
# slot resolver assumes exactly this layout, so a clone that lost it cannot
# reproduce a board the link update works on.
!tools/rp2350-partitions.json
# Post-build step of env rp2350_motion (platformio.ini extra_scripts).
!tools/rp2350_tbyb.py
.clangd
# clangd's index cache — 844 files that get rewritten on every parse. It was
# tracked until 2026-07-29, which is why the repo showed 1249 tracked files
# when only 405 are real.
.cache/
.clang-format
.cache/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Working docs, audits, plans & UI mockups — scratch, not firmware
SD32-*.md
sd32-preview-*.html
waypoint_kinematics_audit.md
graph_screenshot_temp.html
compile_commands.json
NewPCB.md
HANDOFF.md
plan.md
PLAN_NewPCB_Migration.md
PLAN_OSSM_Parity.md

# Reference hardware docs / binaries — not source
PCB Layout.diy
AIM_servo_modbus_reference.md
AIM_Servo_Motor_Datasheet_EN_with_images.pdf

# Build outputs, captures & scratch artifacts — generated, not source.
/build/
sim/slopsim/build/

# Generated channel-grid visual (tools/gen_channel_grid.py)
docs/slopsync/channel-grid.html

# SlopScope diagnostic captures (SlopSync repo's tools/slopscope.py, run
# against this device) — traces and rendered graphs are per-session evidence,
# not source, and land in whatever directory the harness is invoked from.
slopscope-*.jsonl
slopscope-*.html

# SlopSoak run summaries (SlopSync repo's tools/slopsoak.py, run against this
# device) — same reasoning as SlopScope's captures: per-run evidence,
# regenerated by re-running the harness. The baseline numbers that matter are
# quoted in docs/ws-transport-baseline.md.
slopsoak-*.json

# DIR ladder rows (tools/dir_ladder.py) — per-run measurements, regenerated by
# re-running the ladder. Numbers that end up mattering get quoted into
# docs/canon/LEDGER.md, which is where a result becomes a fact.
dir_ladder.json

# webui/test/evidence/ — per-run render screenshots and OG reference shots.
# Regenerated by webui/test/*.mjs on demand; backups cover durability. Tracking
# binaries here bloated the tree once already.
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negations below only work against a contents glob.
webui/test/evidence/*
# ...EXCEPT these two. They are FIXTURES, not evidence: render-vs-samplerate-probe.mjs
# readFileSync()s them as its INPUT, so ignoring them silently breaks that probe
# on a fresh clone. 15 KB of text each, and re-capturing them needs a live device
# at two specific subscribe rates — same reasoning that tracks SlopSync's
# clients/js/test/fixtures/slopsim-catalog.bin. Move them to a fixtures/ dir if
# the naming ever gets confusing enough to be worth the path change.
!webui/test/evidence/trace-25hz.json
!webui/test/evidence/trace-30hz.json

# slopsim async-tune shelf (sim/slopsim/src/machine/RecordingStore.h). The shelf
# now lives OUTSIDE the tree by default (%LOCALAPPDATA%/slopsim/, so a clean
# rebuild cannot delete regression fixtures), but --recordings can point it back
# in here — so the ignore stays. Recordings and runs are per-take working
# material and runs are LARGE (one text row per millisecond). If a specific take
# ever becomes a fixture some check reads, track THAT file by name with a
# negation, the way webui/test/evidence does above.
slopsim-recordings/

# playwright-mcp scratch (page snapshots, console logs, screenshots) — per-run
# evidence from driving the analyzer in a browser, never an input to anything.
.playwright-mcp/

# Deployed-firmware ELF archive. A core dump is a list of ADDRESSES and they only
# mean something against the exact binary that produced them (proved 2026-07-31:
# a real dump symbolized to `bt_bb_gain_set` inside a newlib stdio stack against
# a 2-version-newer ELF). Kept per deployed version so `/api/coredump` stays
# readable — 32 MB each, generated, never source. Back these up, do not commit.
#
# artifacts/ is now the ONE home for ALL per-run output (.claude/rules/
# repo-layout.md): captures, traces, ladders, sweeps, ELF archives. Every
# tools/ script defaults --out here, so results stop landing in the repo root.
artifacts/*
# ...except the anchor. A fresh clone needs the directory to exist because the
# tools write into it without mkdir. Note /* above rather than /: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# Vendor manuals, datasheets and schematics. Reference INPUTS, not artifacts,
# and binary, so they are kept out of the tree the same way. One home instead
# of a per-filename ignore each time a new PDF lands at the root.
docs/reference/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# Generated by tools/gen_logview_header.py as a c5_probe pre-script; never
# hand-edited and never a source of truth.
src/c5_probe/logview_gz.h
